    q: 'Why do brands on Myntra, Flipkart, and Ajio show EU shoe sizes?',
    a: 'Many international brands sold in India—such as Zara, H&M, Adidas, Puma, and Mango—use European sizing as their primary manufacturing standard. Always verify whether a product page lists sizes in "EU" or "UK/India" before ordering.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I convert European women’s shoe sizes to Indian sizes?',
    a: 'To convert an EU women’s shoe size to Indian sizing, subtract approximately 33 from the European size (for example, EU 38 − 33 = India 5; EU 39 − 33 = India 6). For half sizes, cross-reference foot length in centimeters.'
